### Hypothesis assessment at code level

  Q: Does compute_team_ev use bookmaker marginal probabilities directly
     (independence-assuming)?
  A: YES. Line 730-731 reads pre-computed `total_ev` per rider (= sum of
     finish_ev/sprint_ev/gc_ev/jersey_ev/kom_ev marginals from build_probabilities).
     Line 733 adds `max(total_evs)` as captain bonus. Line 734 adds team_bonus_ev.
     Line 735-736 adds depth_bonus from `round(sum(top15))` — sums marginal top-15 probs
     into a single expected-top-15-count integer and looks up DEPTH_BONUS table.
     NO modelling of which rider actually finishes 1st vs 2nd vs ... in joint dist.

  Q: Does simulate_stage sample stage outcomes with mutual-exclusivity preserved?
  A: YES. Plackett-Luce scoring at line 1920-1923:
       u      = rng.uniform(1e-12, 1.0, (n_sims, n_field))
       scores = -log(u) / field_probs   # one score per (sim, rider)
       order  = argsort(scores, axis=1) # argsort → finish order per sim
     Exactly ONE rider gets each finish position per simulation. Per-position points
     (FINISH_POINTS table) are accumulated only for the rider at that position.
     n_sims=10,000 joint realizations across the full ~170-rider field.

  → Hypothesis CONFIRMED at code level:
    - compute_team_ev independence-assuming marginal sum
    - simulate_stage joint-distribution Plackett-Luce MC
    - SA loops invoke compute_team_ev (line 1031); displayed Net EV uses simulate_stage
    - These are genuinely different EV formulations.

